    "body": "Support configuring the width of the preview window specifically for files. I wanted the preview window for files to be larger, so I decided to add the `width_file_preview` option. However, setting this (or any other width option) to a large value can make the windows overlap each other, which didn't seem intended to me. Thus, I also added some calculations to reset the widths of the created windows to fit the vim width. This change can be separated out into its own PR if desired, but put them both here as I felt the context was helpful.\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n",
    "closed_at": "2025-10-26T08:26:13Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\n\nThe \"resize in proportion\" is not something I think should be done in 'mini.files'. This breaks config which defines widths *exactly*. If the window doesn't fit, it should be not shown. If this is not happening right now after the file preview option, then something is wrong in the other part of the code.\n\nAlso, 'mini.files' is already quite big and the threshold for any new features/configs is \"*very* low line count compared to their effect\". I am still debating whether a separate file preview width fits this.\n\nIn the meantime I think I am going to close this. Thank you for your time and effort, though!",
