            "body": "> > If this is not happening right now after the file preview option, then something is wrong in the other part of the code.\r\n> \r\n> so the behavior right now is if only the focused window and the preview window exist, if the config is such that the there is not enough space for the preview window, the preview window keeps the size but stays under the focused window overlapping and hiding it. what do you believe the expected behavior should be here?\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce this. The preview window is omitted completely if it doesn't fit the screen (thus only focused window remains). If you can provide reproduction steps for window overlapping, please create an issue.\r\n\r\n> on your note about contributions, would code cleanup be welcome like adding types (no functionality change)\r\n\r\nType annotations are currently mostly used for 'mini.doc' documentation. Going beyond that is not (currently) planned. So more rigorous typing is not something I'd like to see in 'mini.nvim' (yet). There are some more thoughts in [this comment](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/1110#issuecomment-2266660524).",
